# APML Interface: Self-Explaining Dashboard (compiled explainer)
# SSI Learning App
# Version: 1.1.0 (2026-07-29) — How-this-works = single surfacing point (walks + invitations in the panel) with a discoverability throb
# Status: Live on node home (admin + leader member mounts). Design doc: docs/self-explaining-dashboard.md

## ============================================================================
## OVERVIEW
## ============================================================================

SPECIFICATION:
  name: "Self-Explaining Dashboard"
  purpose: "Docs, training, onboarding and feature-discovery as ONE act: the system explaining itself from live state, per persona. Compiled once (CLI, tokens at refresh time), rendered forever (static pack, zero runtime LLM)."
  compiler: "tools/explainer/compile.mjs (+ rulings/*.md, rules.json — the hand-maintained DECISIONS)"
  pack: "packages/player-vue/src/explainer/pack.json (versioned, bundled; human render docs/explainer-pack.md)"
  runtime: "packages/player-vue/src/explainer/evaluateRules.ts + useNoticingInvitations.ts (ONE evaluation per page) + components/admin/{HowThisWorks,NoticingInvitations}.vue"
  surface: "NodeHomeView.vue — admin mount (/admin/groups|schools|classes/:id) persona=admin; member mount (/schools/org/:id) persona=leader"
  learner_level: "DELIBERATELY NOTHING — the player must need no explanation (founder ruling)"

DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY:
  one_line: "A compiler, not a stale cache and not a per-user concierge."
  principles:
    - "Decisions vs derivables: only rulings (persona prose) and rules (noticing conditions) are hand-maintained; the pack and its truth manifest regenerate."
    - "DRIFT GATE: compile FAILS when an explanation names a verb the surface lost, or a rule reads a field home.ts stopped emitting — staleness becomes a build failure."
    - "Noticing rules are pure data over stats the page ALREADY fetched — no new queries, no polling, no runtime model calls."
    - "Invitations, not missions: gentle, dismissible (14d per rule×node, localStorage), never modal, max 3, deep links resolve member/admin-correct via nodeSurfacePaths."
    - "SINGLE SURFACING POINT (founder ruling 2026-07-29): the How-this-works button surfaces ANY invitation for the persona×place — its panel lists the explanation, the current noticing invitations (compact rows) and the walk offers."

DISCOVERABILITY_THROB:
  ruling: "founder 2026-07-29: 'glow/throb on first visit, throb again if the app thinks that somethings haven't been used/done yet — subtle so that it doesn't trap attention, but make it discoverable super easily'"
  state: "src/explainer/howThisWorksThrob.ts — localStorage 'ssi-htw-seen', entries `${viewerId}:node-home:${nodeId}` = {seenAt, invKeys}, pruned 180d; viewerId = auth uid ('anon' until session resolves)"
  arm: "first visit = viewer has NO seen entry for the surface; re-arm = current undismissed invitation set contains a key not recorded at the last panel open of this node"
  disarm: "opening the panel = markSeen(current keys); dismissal shrinking the set never re-arms"
  render: "6px soft-pulsing dot beside the link (2.6s opacity 0.35↔0.85) + link one shade darker; prefers-reduced-motion → static dot, no animation; never modal, never auto-plays (startWalk stays tap-only)"
  tests: "src/explainer/howThisWorksThrob.test.ts"

## ============================================================================
## CONTRACTS
## ============================================================================

PACK_SHAPE:
  version: "12-hex content hash"
  truth: "verbs (parsed from NodeActionBar.vue + See insights), statWords (NodeHomeView), measures+windows (rate-compare.ts)"
  explanations: "persona (admin|leader|school_admin|teacher) × kind (group|school|class) — markdown-lite (**bold** only)"
  rules: "NoticingRule[] — shapes node | perChild | countWhere; conditions {path, op(eq|gt|lt|gte|lte|truthy|falsy), value}; cta targets insights | lens:classes | child-home | students"

RULES_V1:
  silent_class: "class practised before, zero sessions this week → insights"
  quiet_subtree: "classes below, none practised this week → lens:classes"
  school_no_teachers: "school child with zero teachers → that school's home (per child, cap 3)"
  students_quiet_week: "previously-active students silent this week in an active class → in-page (students list)"

KIND_RESOLUTION:
  rule: "payload kind 'class' wins; else the node's OWN label decides (label-not-type — a school attachment never outvotes the label); unlabelled falls back to commercial/hasSchool"

WIRING_STATUS:
  wired: "admin, leader (NodeHomeView both mounts)"
  authored_not_wired: "school_admin, teacher — wire when legacy /schools surfaces converge onto node home (THE-VIEW §4)"
  telemetry_input: "v2 stub (--telemetry flag prints stub notice; no signal before its consumer)"

TESTS:
  unit: "src/explainer/evaluateRules.test.ts — evaluator ops, all four rules' fire paths, caps, persona/kind scoping, member links, pack integrity"
  live: "src/explainer/verifyIme.live.test.ts (IME_LIVE=1, network) — redeems the IME leader personal link on deployed dev, walks the full IME subtree (~24 nodes), asserts every rule's fire/no-fire against the live values"
